  "access_terms": "BMRB states community data are publicly available free of charge. No explicit redistribution license is assumed. Fetch original data locally into ignored .artifacts; do not commit or redistribute the acquisitions.",
  "reference_software": "TopSpin 2.1, independently deposited processing and audit trail from April 2011",
  "protocol": {
    "declared_before_raw_comparison": true,
    "calibration": "No peak-fitted shifts, reversals or gain. Archive ppm grid OFFSET - index*SW_p/(SF*SI); raw frequency axis calibrated with (SFO1-SF)*1e6/SF from acquisition and corresponding archived processing SF.",
    "normalization": "Independent archived processed integer intensities scaled by 2**NC_proc. Raw-to-reference volumes compared as within-spectrum region ratios, canceling arbitrary receiver/FFT gain; no per-region gain fits.",
    "volume_measure": "Signed 2D trapezoid in physical Hz, baseline none; multilinear interpolation at fixed ppm rectangle endpoints; no peak-height substitution.",
    "volume_tolerance": "Processed-reference integration relative error <=1e-10 against separate NumPy array quadrature. Raw-to-TopSpin region-ratio relative error <=0.30 is a predeclared, coarse processing comparison, never absolute concentration validation.",
    "positive_peak_truth": "Strong listed HSQC1JCH peaks are the predeclared main gate; all curated rows are retained, including the third weak LR entry as supplemental signal-neighborhood diagnostics. Unlisted signals are not counted as false positives. TOCSY uses predeclared multiplet rectangles and independent archived maxima, not a curated TOCSY peak list.",
    "limitations": [
      "Two acquisition cases from one compound and one instrument, not a broad independent cohort.",
      "TopSpin processing differs in digital-filter/phase/apodization details. Raw ratio gate is coarse, not amplitude or full-array parity.",
      "Archive has no quantified peak volumes. Integration correctness uses the independent immutable processed reference array as numerical oracle; volumes do not certify concentration.",
      "First-order automatic phase may be unidentifiable because these small molecule peaks span a narrow fraction of the full sweep."
    ],
    "raw_apodization": "Exponential on each axis, lb_hz = log(100)/(pi*(original_raw_axis.size-1)*original_raw_axis.step), computed only from the ORIGINAL acquisition grid before digital-filter trimming. The target exponential factor is 1% at the original final acquisition time. After 69 direct samples are trimmed, actual retained direct endpoint factors are 1.8623389% for HSQC and 1.3642607% for TOCSY; indirect factors remain 1%. First-point scale 0.5 is a separate additional weight on each axis: the endpoint exponential factor is not the ratio to that weighted first point (that ratio is twice the endpoint factor). Parameters remain unchanged after trimming. This differs from archived squared-cosine windows.",
    "phase_policy": "HSQC both-axis zero-order (first_order=false), since its only two isolated peaks span <15% of each sweep and cannot identify slopes. TOCSY both-axis zero/first-order (first_order=true), including reference-standard resonances selected without consulting archived peak positions. No TopSpin phase parameters used for automatic estimation.",
    "peak_position_tolerance": "Raw positive ROI maximum vs independently archived positive ROI maximum <=2 processed bins per axis; this accommodates discretization and apodization shift within the fixed multiplet rectangle. Curated HSQC peak-list locations are separately checked within the same2bin tolerance; no omitted-peak false-positive assertion.",
    "ratio_tolerance_rationale": "30% is a conservative predeclared engineering acceptance budget for finite fixed rectangles under different apodization and fitted phase policies, not a confidence interval or claimed measurement accuracy. The 128 complex indirect increments and an exponential window targeting 1% on the original acquisition grid (retained direct endpoints 1.8623389% HSQC / 1.3642607% TOCSY) broaden lines relative to the archived WDW4 SSB2 processing; signed tails leak across fixed rectangle boundaries. Within-spectrum ratios cancel arbitrary global gain but do not cancel region-dependent tails or phase errors. Report actual errors so readers can choose a stricter application-specific budget."
  },
